    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "London-based computational design studio founded 2012 by Marcin Ignac (founder, lead creative; background in computer science, new media art, interaction design; ex-CIID, ex-Shiftcontrol) and Damien Seguin (tech lead, computational designer; ex-UNIT9; studied at Gobelins Paris). Core output: generative art, data visualisation, bespoke interactive tools, and large-scale immersive installations. Clients include Google, Twitter, Nike, IBM, Monotype, Wellcome Trust, Dropbox, GSK, H&M. Built their own open-source 3D engine (PEX) and internal design tool (Nodes.io). Studio-level entity; two named principals doing deep hands-on code-driven creative work. Size pre-set as 11-40 in Notion but multiple sources (LinkedIn, studio page) indicate 2-10; corrected to 2-10.",
      "source_url": null,
      "verified_at": "2026-07-13T10:06:43",
      "set_by": "agent"
    },
